content.text:
The page and its design language are now saved on this laptop:

- **The page:** commit `1649980` in git (`gui/start.js`, `gui/start.css`). Think of a commit as a numbered snapshot of the files.
- **The design language:** a new file, `gui/DESIGN.md`, committed as `02663dd`. It covers:
  - the 8 colors and when to use each;
  - the type rules (light, tight big titles; bold uppercase labels);
  - square corners, hairline rules and the left/right grid;
  - how the stripes are drawn (10 px each, touching, never crossing, offsets along the curve);
  - the motion values (springs with damping 1.0 and about 0.45 s);
  - a short "don't" list (no BMW logo, no extra colors, no rounded corners or shadows).

  Teammates and other AI agents get it through the GUI README, which now links to it.
- **My memory:** a note so future sessions know this style is approved and must be used for the graph page and the mid-process page.

Both commits have their Entire checkpoint.

So far everything exists only on this laptop. A push uploads the branch to GitHub so it's backed up and the team can see it. The hand-off said to wait for your OK. Should I push `feat/pm-inbox` now? It doesn't change `main`, which is what the judges see.
